From: Nura rc4k series <rc4k@nura.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: guacamole: enable the NQ330 NFC bus

Use the project 18821 vendor DTBO wiring on QUP SE9, with the mainline
NXP NCI binding. Keep the bus at 100 kHz and drop its disabled GPI DMA
provider references, matching the board's other FIFO-mode I2C buses.
GPIO42 belongs to the secure element and must remain untouched.

This enables probe and ROM-mode reader experiments only. Reference-clock
support and board-specific NCI configuration remain hardware-test gates;
a successful probe does not establish RF operation. No firmware download
or secure-element support is enabled.

The IRQ pin is pulled down, not up as in the vendor DTBO. nxp-nci holds
VEN low from probe and requests the level-high IRQ at once; with the chip
off, a pull-up keeps GPIO47 asserted. That gave ~226k IRQ/s on CPU0 with
every read NACKed (-121), starving UFS UIC completion so clock scaling
failed with -110. The vendor nq-nci driver only enabled its IRQ after
powering the chip, which hid the problem on Android.

Nura-Category: device-dt
Nura-Origin: guacamole stock project 18821 DTBO; docs/NFC_FEASIBILITY.md
Upstream-Status: candidate
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
@@ -675,3 +675,47 @@
 };
 
 #include "sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-displayport.dtsi"
+
+/* NQ330 NCI controller; leave the eSE power GPIO42 unclaimed. */
+&tlmm {
+	nfc_int_default: nfc-int-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio47";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-down;
+	};
+
+	nfc_enable_default: nfc-enable-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio41", "gpio48";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	nfc_clk_req_default: nfc-clk-req-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio113";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+		input-enable;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c9 {
+	status = "okay";
+	clock-frequency = <100000>;
+	/delete-property/ dmas;
+	/delete-property/ dma-names;
+
+	nfc: nfc@28 {
+		compatible = "nxp,pn553", "nxp,nxp-nci-i2c";
+		reg = <0x28>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&tlmm>;
+		interrupts = <47 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 41 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		firmware-gpios = <&tlmm 48 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&nfc_int_default>, <&nfc_enable_default>,
+			    <&nfc_clk_req_default>;
+	};
+};
